  "description": "Change of use of the first and second floors from\r\nOffice (Use Class E(g)(i)) to 4no. flats (1 x 3-bed, 2 x 2-bed and 1 x 1-bed)\r\n(Use Class C3); extension and retention of the existing ground floor to provide\r\nan enlarged flexible commercial unit (Use Class E); single and two-storey rear\r\nextensions; second-floor rear extension; alterations to the roof to form an\r\nenlarged rear dormer; alterations to the roof of the second-floor extension;\r\nrooflights to the front and both side roof slopes; installation of a biodiverse\r\nroof to the proposed single-storey rear extension; cycle and refuse stores; and\r\nassociated external alterations",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to deliver an appropriate mix of dwelling sizes. This fails to deliver larger family-sized units (3 bedrooms or more) which is the required mix of unit sizes needed to meet local housing needs and results in an over‑concentration of smaller units contrary to the requirements of the Harrow Local Plan. As submitted, the scheme would provide a housing offer that is unduly skewed towards smaller homes and does not support local demand for family accommodation, undermining sustainable community objectives. The application therefore conflicts with Policies D3 and D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policies HO1 and HO2 of Harrow Local Plan 2021 – 2041 and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of the poor outlook to units on the second floor, compromised daylight and sunlight to internal and habitable spaces, lack of private amenity spaces, poor siting, insufficient and cramped refuse store, poor access would result in poor quality accommodation which would not be fit for purpose, to the detriment of the residential amenities of the future occupiers, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 (7), D5, D7 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), and Policies GR1, GR3A, HO2, of the Harrow&amp;nbsp; Local Plan (2021 - 2041).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Car parking cannot be satisfactorily provided within the curtilage of the site to meet the Council&#x27;s requirements in respect of the development, and there are no avenues for on- street parking in the neighbouring highways which would be detrimental to the free flow and safety on the neighbouring highways and the amenity of neighbouring residents, contrary to National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy T6 of The London Plan (2021), Policies GR1 and M2 of Harrow Local Plan (2021 - 2041) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
